      ":question/id": "812ba011-0257-5cc3-a9ad-5565226f48f4",
      ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -8 & -8 \\\\ -9 & 7 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{12}=0$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3}.\n$$\n\nAt the requested entry, this gives\n\n$$\na_{12}=-8+(-2)\\cdot (-4)=0.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A &=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -8 & -8 \\\\ -9 & 7 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-14 & 0 & -22 \\\\ -9 & 7 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
