      ":question/problem": "Given that\n$$\nX = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{21} = 0$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\nR_{2}:=R_{2} + R_{1}.\n$$\n\nAt the requested entry, this gives\n\n$$\na_{21}=-1+(1)\\cdot (1)=0.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad R_{2}:=R_{2} + R_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\nR_{2}:=R_{2} + R_{1}.\n$$",
